Mandarin pronunciation
----------------------

Chinese is pronounced by kempelen's own front end (crates/kempelen/src/phonemes/chinese),
a port of the one Kokoro's Chinese voices were trained with. It uses, as source
ideas or data:

- misaki (Apache-2.0), by hexgrad: the sound table and punctuation rules.
  https://github.com/hexgrad/misaki
- pinyin-to-ipa (MIT), by Stefan Taubert, which misaki adapts: the
  syllable-to-sound mapping.
- pypinyin (MIT), by mozillazg, and the pinyin-data and phrase-pinyin-data it is
  built from (MIT): the character and phrase readings in
  crates/kempelen/mandarin. https://github.com/mozillazg/python-pinyin
- cn2an (MIT), by Ailln: the rules for reading numbers in Chinese.
  https://github.com/Ailln/cn2an
- OpenCC (Apache-2.0), by BYVoid: TSCharacters.txt, the table that writes
  Traditional characters as Simplified ones (crates/kempelen/mandarin).
  https://github.com/BYVoid/OpenCC
- jieba (MIT), by fxsjy: the word dictionary, through the jieba-rs crate (MIT),
  by messense, a dependency.

The data files are generated by crates/kempelen/mandarin/export.py and checked
against misaki's own output in the tests (crates/kempelen/tests/golden).

