Downloaded, not shipped
-----------------------

Neither of these is in the repository or in a program built from it:

- The Kokoro-82M v1.0 ONNX model and voices (Apache-2.0; publisher
  onnx-community, upstream hexgrad/Kokoro-82M). The caller stages them; the
  pinned revision, sizes and SHA-256 digests are in
  crates/kempelen/assets/speech-assets.json, which also fetches the model's
  licence and model card. kempelen never downloads them at synthesis time.
- The optional CUDA runtime (feature cuda-install): pyke's ONNX Runtime CUDA
  provider and NVIDIA's CUDA, cuBLAS, cuFFT and cuDNN libraries, downloaded only
  when the caller asks, and kept under NVIDIA's and pyke's own terms.

ONNX Runtime itself is linked through the ort and ort-sys crates (MIT OR
Apache-2.0; the runtime MIT, by Microsoft). A program that ships kempelen must
carry their notices with its other dependencies' licences.
